Z||000008||fiero56||01-02-2001||01:41 AM||||Guess I am just one of the few people who are glad that body design never made it to production. Pontiac could have saved millions from design teams by making a Firebird and slapping "Fiero" somewhere on it, and calling it "a new Fiero." There is very little difference between that and Firebird. <P>If Pontiac would have continued Fiero production, I know exactly what would have happened. Pontiac would have eventually slapped too many bells and whistles, and made the car so fat and expensive, it never would have made it. Just like the Supra, RX7, 300ZX, 3000GT, and others. They all got too much crap on them, were too expensive, and died off. I'm pretty sure same thing would have happened to Fiero. I think t-tops and a/c were nearing the limit.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Notchit||01-02-2001||04:35 AM||||I agree, they would have made the car so expensive that no one could afford it...I like the 80's style, that one looks sweet, but not exotic enough, maybe thats just me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||4
Z||000010||jlhuber||01-02-2001||09:15 AM||||it does kinda look like a firebird except for a few items.  it has some styling cues of the fiero (i.e. side intake, front fascia, rear quarter windows).  to the best of my knowledge, the production firebird has always had 4 seats.  the car pictured above clearly has only two.  how do i come up with this you say?  look at the rear window area in the second picture, it is the same as the 86-88gt with the quarter windows and simulated (read: look at it from the side) fastback styling.  now with the rear window like that and the probability that it has a mid/rear engine, as cued by the side intake, there is nowhere to put a rear seat.  therefore you only have a two seat sports car made by gm, and it sure does not look like a 'vette to me.  but i do agree that it is probably best it was never built, keeps us all dreaming.  also, when you get too many luxuries or "creature comforts" as they are called, they do tend to get a wee bit more expensive than most people are willing to pay.  all in all, i do like the prototype's styling.  if someone were to make a kit car styled body of it, with a few modifications (namely the rear fascia) i would buy one.  but what are the chances of that eh?  ah well, live and learn.<p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 01-02-2001).]||||reg||1
