Z||000024||kslish||01-03-2001||03:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>The rear end is also a bit too long..  for a little comparison I overlayed a pic of a Fastback GT onto the side shot..<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, but I bet the trunk space in the GTP is almost twice as big as it is in our '84-'88 Fieros. I do agree that the rear overhang may be a bit much though. <P>What the designers were clearly going after was to make the GTP look like the sucessful Fiero GTP racecars of the late '80s that had a longer rear end to improve high speed aerodynamics....here is a pic of the Fiero racecar:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPracer.jpg">  <P>Also if you want to check out the test mules for the '89 coupe and Formula, search for a past thread on this forum about them or go to:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/wpfc/89discovery.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/wpfc/89discovery.html</A> <P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR>||||reg||1
